\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two operators with one coordinate action}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Conjugation by an invertible operator and by its negative gives
the same result. A spin space can therefore distinguish two
operators that act identically on directions. To find out whether
the ambiguity extends beyond this sign, start with the operators
for reversing a direction and for turning a pair of directions.}
